        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="1309" n="1213" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1213"/>

                <head>No. 804.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Russell to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation at Caracas</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1874-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            13, 1874</date>. (Received August 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit the reply of
                    the late minister of foreign relations to a communication of the United States
                    minister resident, protesting against a law of Venezuela punishing false claims
                    on the treasury. The reply is marked 2, and is accompanied by a translation.</p>
                <p>Perhaps it is proper for me to suggest that, as Mr. Pile’s letter was of
                    September, 1873, and as the reply bears date of January 18, and as both
                    governments have stated their views, no object can be attained by making any
                    rejoinder to the reply of the Venezuelan minister.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>THOMAS RUSSELL.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d807-a1.xml" xpointer="d807-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d807-a2.xml" xpointer="d807-a2"/>
